id: tornado-weather
name: Tornado Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
profile: elemental-wind
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The wind. Speeds and Defense Value 2(WT) lower, and past Natural it halves your
  Haste. At Cataclysmic it drags everybody towards an epicenter, which is the table's.
text: >
  Tornado Weather: Strong, cyclical winds lift the terrain and block visibility,
  buffering you around the battlefield.

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Wind)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * Reduce your Speeds and Defense Value by 2(WT).

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * Halve your Haste.

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * Upon the creation of this Battle Weather, the creator (ARC or otherwise) will select
  a point within the Battle Weather to be the epicenter. At the start of each Combat
  Round, you are moved 3 Squares towards the epicenter in the most direct path possible
  (if any Feature or Character is in the way, then proceed to follow the typical rules
  for Collision - see Battlefields).

---

# The third Weather, and the first whose top Tier is not a number.
#
# --- Natural (1) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce your Speeds and Defense Value by 2(WT)."
#
# Your Speeds - both of them, Normal and Boosted - so this writes to `speed.all` rather
# than to the two by name. A file that knew how many Speeds there are is a file that would
# have to be found again if there were ever a third.
#
# 2(WT), so it is 2 at Natural and 6 at Cataclysmic. The Defense Value carries into the
# Dodge Roll, which is where most of this will actually be felt.
#
# --- Unnatural (2) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Halve your Haste."
#
# Haste feeds the Strike Roll, so this is the attacking half of the same idea: the wind
# takes the Defense at Natural and the Strike at Unnatural. A multiplication on the
# finished value, like every other halving here.
#
# --- Cataclysmic (3) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You are moved 3 Squares towards the epicenter in the most direct path possible."
#
# Not built, and not buildable here. Every noun in it is one this system does not have: an
# epicenter is a point on a map, "3 Squares towards" is a distance and a direction, and
# "the most direct path possible" is a route through whatever is standing in it. This
# system moves nobody and measures nothing.
#
# So the Tier is real and its effect is the table's, which is the same answer Scale and
# Replacing Weathers already get. What is worth saying is that the one part of it that does
# reach a character is already built: "proceed to follow the typical rules for Collision"
# is the Receive Collision Damage button on the Battlefields tab, and whoever is dragged
# into something presses it.
#
# Deliberately not written as a start-of-round block that does nothing. A block that fires
# and changes no value is indistinguishable from a broken one, and it would put Tornado
# Weather's third Tier in the same shape as Hot and Cold's - which it is not.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Wind)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles, and
# there are none in this system yet. Carried in the header and read by nobody.

[passive]
speed.all -= 2(WT);
defenseValue -= 2(WT);

if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
  haste *= 0.5;
}
